  "context_pill": "Section 44AE Presumptive Taxation",
  "example_summary": "Computation of presumptive business income for Mr. X operating goods vehicles during P.Y. 2025-26 under Section 44AE.",
  "source_provision": "| Category | Statutory Provision | Operative Threshold / Rate | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Eligible Assessee** | Section 44AE(1) | Owning not more than **10 goods vehicles** at any time during the previous year | Can opt for presumptive income computation |\n| **Heavy Goods Vehicle** | Section 44AE(2)(i) | Gross vehicle weight **exceeds 12,000 kg** | **₹ 1,000 per ton** of gross vehicle weight / unladen weight per month or part of month |\n| **Other Goods Carriage** | Section 44AE(2)(ii) | Gross vehicle weight **not exceeding 12,000 kg** | **₹ 7,500 per month** or part of month for each vehicle |\n| **Ownership Period** | Section 44AE(7) | Calculated for each month or part of the month the vehicle is owned | Actual utilization or date of put to use does **not** restrict the ownership period calculation |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Threshold Limit Rule:\n> If the assessee owns more than **10 goods vehicles** at any time during the previous year, Section 44AE cannot be applied, and regular books of account must be maintained under Section 44AA and audited under Section 44AB.\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Partial Month Rule:\n> Any part of a month during which the vehicle is owned by the assessee must be considered as a full month for computing presumptive business income under Section 44AE.",
